  "rationale": "Every exfiltrate technique needs admin on db, fileserver or backup. Getting that admin needs a foothold there, which needs stolen_dbadmin. stolen_dbadmin needs admin_dc or admin_adfs. Those need a foothold on dc or adfs plus stolen_admin. stolen_admin comes only from kerberoasting, which needs a foothold on appserver or apiserver. That foothold needs reach_internal and stolen_user. The shortest chain is: 1 phish_workstation (gives foothold_workstation and stolen_user), 2 pivot_internal, 3 auth_appserver, 4 kerberoast_dc, 5 auth_dc, 6 escalate_dc, 7 dump_dbadmin_dc, 8 auth_db, 9 escalate_db, 10 exfiltrate_db. Each step is the only way to satisfy a precondition of a later step, and the alternative branches (adfs, fileserver, backup) are the same length, so no shorter path exists."
